---
import Arrow from "../components/Arrow.astro";
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import Brand from "../components/Brand.astro";
import ContactBand from "../components/ContactBand.astro";
---

<Base
  title="Warehouse solutions"
  description="Explore zone picking, multi-order transport, and material movement with packsel warehouse automation for 3PLs."
>
  <section class="container page-intro">
    <p class="kicker">Solutions for 3PL warehouses</p>
    <h1>
      Move the work.
      <br />
      Free up your people.
    </h1>
    <p class="lead">
      <Brand tm /> helps you design automation around the trips, handoffs, and
      picking tasks that fill your day.
    </p>
  </section>
  <div class="container">
    <img
      class="wide-photo"
      src="/images/warehouse-robots.webp"
      width="1440"
      height="960"
      alt="packsel shelf robots in a fulfillment aisle"
    />
    <p class="note">
      Product visualization. Final configurations and workflows are defined with
      your team.
    </p>
  </div>
  <section class="container section-large">
    <article class="solution-row">
      <div>
        <p class="kicker">01 / Zone picking</p>
        <h2>
          Bring the orders
          <br />
          to the associate.
        </h2>
      </div>
      <div class="stack">
        <p class="lead">
          Give each associate a focused zone. Robots move between those zones,
          collecting items for multiple orders before heading to packing.
        </p>
        <ul class="simple-list">
          <li>
            Plan zones around your locations, order profile, and pick density.
          </li>
          <li>
            Guide picks with SKU, quantity, location, and barcode confirmation.
          </li>
          <li>
            Keep orders in separate bins and define client separation rules.
          </li>
        </ul>
        <a class="text-link" href="/warehouse-demo/index.html">
          Explore the illustrative workflow <Arrow />
        </a>
      </div>
    </article>
    <article class="solution-row">
      <div>
        <p class="kicker">02 / Order transport</p>
        <h2>
          Let picked orders
          <br />
          make their own trip.
        </h2>
      </div>
      <div class="stack">
        <p class="lead">
          Reduce the need for associates to leave their work area to move totes
          and completed picks between stations.
        </p>
        <ul class="simple-list">
          <li>Define pickup, packing, and return locations.</li>
          <li>Choose shelf and tote arrangements for your order mix.</li>
          <li>Design clear handoffs for loading, unloading, and exceptions.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </article>
    <article class="solution-row">
      <div>
        <p class="kicker">03 / Material movement</p>
        <h2>
          Take repeat trips
          <br />
          off the task list.
        </h2>
      </div>
      <div class="stack">
        <p class="lead">
          Look beyond picking. Repeated point-to-point transport may be another
          place to put a mobile robot to work.
        </p>
        <ul class="simple-list">
          <li>Move materials between defined workstations.</li>
          <li>Assess replenishment and return transport routes.</li>
          <li>Match platform or shelf configurations to the load.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </article>
  </section>
  <section class="surface-sunken section-large">
    <div class="container split">
      <div class="stack">
        <p class="kicker">Fit comes first</p>
        <h2>
          Designed around
          <br />
          your reality.
        </h2>
        <p class="lead">
          Your layout, systems, and operating patterns determine what should be
          automated.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="feature-lines">
        <div>
          <span class="mono">01</span>
          <p>
            <strong>Floor and traffic</strong>
            <br />
            Aisle widths, crossings, floor conditions, and pedestrian routes.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <span class="mono">02</span>
          <p>
            <strong>Orders and inventory</strong>
            <br />
            Pick density, item sizes, client rules, and peak demand.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <span class="mono">03</span>
          <p>
            <strong>Systems and connectivity</strong>
            <br />
            WMS API access, location data, scanners, and Wi-Fi coverage.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <ContactBand />
</Base>
